{"title":"2021 CJMC Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CJMC_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Right angled triangle ABC has its right angle at C, side AC has length 9 cm and side BC has length 12 cm. Points D and E are on AC so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/6/9967b272252127b1154cd4b8036f8667af5758ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=DE=EC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"138\" height=\"14\" />. Similarly, points F and G are on AB so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/2/9c2f2ad55c958044890f2f9f7062e30b275fa1ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF=FG=GB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"136\" height=\"14\" />. What is the area of trapezoid DFGE?\n</p><p>(A) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41e1d1ea5dbaa033267ae0c59d25184d91c3da06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9\\text{ cm}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />\n(B) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be01574e276fd5a9ae74cba0dce9058d4b78b4c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12\\text{ cm}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />\n(C) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/8/0b8df09b47629971cad30af55f96a31c33be8d4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15\\text{ cm}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />\n(D) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/6/716eefe1543e87ddc9ead30846f317f194d1efc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18\\text{ cm}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />\n(E) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/3/98383a46280b9d74e7178546308329483488c594.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27\\text{ cm}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CJMC_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e728a789f2ca839593526b82229b72fde61ec6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADF$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/3/723998405b9fbb46906c9c76e269e18c4e3934e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AEG$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e5170b3a48d96da708932026f0e94194f415b0b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACB$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> are similar. \n</p><p>The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/f/4fffc0801edc19690232d693bb09a255c50a6c5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 9 \\times 12 = 54\\text{ cm}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"246\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Using the area ratios of similar triangles:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/4/3747f233f8e5d4c7009ad8ffbb27f1e9a762eee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AEG = \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^2 \\times 54 = 24\\text{ cm}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"248\" height=\"48\" /></li>\n<li>Area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/f/dbfa72c3429f52c53d49f0e2d78c40869b6ee92e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADF = \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^2 \\times 54 = 6\\text{ cm}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"240\" height=\"48\" /></li></ul>\n<p>The area of trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/c/60c2f2f23122c4ccbe280125fe871725a633b31f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DFGE = 24 - 6 = 18\\text{ cm}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"211\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><b>Answer:</b> <b>(D)</b>~princepenguin_V\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CJMC_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CJMC_Problems\" title=\"2021 CJMC Problems\">2021 CJMC Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Canada_Jay_Mathematical_Competition\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Canada Jay Mathematical Competition\">Canada Jay Mathematical Competition</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CJMC_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2021 CJMC Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CJMC_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2021 CJMC Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018014734\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.065 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 78/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2659/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:38037:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018014734 and revision id 293634. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}